            {
              "id": "4b49ee2d-b316-3ba0-a06c-01e2ece8e318",
              "name": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the code copies a string literal into a destination buffer using a function that does not guarantee null-termination if the buffer size is reached, and there is no explicit check to ensure the destination pointer is not null before the operation. The risk is further increased because the destination pointer may be null at runtime, which could lead to undefined behavior or a crash. The source is a string literal, which is safe, but the absence of a null check on the destination pointer is a significant concern. There is also no explicit null-termination of the destination buffer after the copy, which could lead to string handling issues. The classification and verdict both indicate a high-confidence, actionable issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore copying the string, ensure that the destination pointer is not null to prevent undefined behavior. Also, explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer after the copy to avoid unterminated strings if the source string is longer than the buffer size.\n\n```c\nif (info && info->vram_vendor) {\n    strncpy(info->vram_vendor, \"UNKNOWN\", AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH);\n    info->vram_vendor[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\nThis approach prevents null pointer dereference and ensures the destination string is always null-terminated, even if the source string is truncated.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n\n___\n"
              },
