            {
              "id": "aff4f22c-8635-3534-9d43-33bdc7de302c",
              "name": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the buffer copy operation. The code copies data from one buffer to another using a function that does not support overlapping memory regions. The analysis determined that the source and destination may refer to overlapping memory areas based on data flow analysis. Additionally, there is no explicit check to ensure that the destination pointer is not null, which could also lead to undefined behavior. The absence of a null-terminator assignment after the copy further increases the risk of string-related issues. These factors indicate a real risk of undefined behavior and potential security vulnerabilities.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nBefore performing the buffer copy, ensure that the source and destination memory regions do not overlap. Add a runtime check to verify that the memory areas are distinct. If overlap is possible, avoid using functions that do not support overlapping regions.\n\n```cpp\nif (info->vram_vendor != brand &&\n    ((brand + AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH <= info->vram_vendor) ||\n     (info->vram_vendor + AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH <= brand))) {\n    strncpy(info->vram_vendor, brand, AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH);\n    info->vram_vendor[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0';\n} else {\n    // Handle overlap case appropriately, e.g., use memmove or log an error\n}\n```\n\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nIf it is possible that the source and destination memory regions overlap, use a function that safely handles overlapping memory, such as `memmove`, instead of `strncpy`. Also, ensure null-termination after the copy.\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(info->vram_vendor, brand, AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH);\ninfo->vram_vendor[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0';\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n\n___\n"
