              "id": "0f050bab-d8f8-3792-9fa3-e3c6dba22c10",
              "name": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the code copies a string from a potentially null source pointer to a potentially null destination pointer without any explicit checks to ensure that either pointer is valid. The classification indicates a risk of undefined behavior due to possible null pointer dereference. The source is a C-style string, which increases the likelihood of a real issue if the object or pointer is not properly initialized. There are no guards in place to check for null pointers before the copy operation, and neither the source nor the destination is guaranteed to be non-null. The function does not ensure that the destination buffer is large enough, nor does it guarantee null-termination after the copy. All these factors contribute to a high confidence that this is a real and actionable issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore copying the string, add explicit checks to ensure that both the source and destination pointers are not null. This prevents undefined behavior due to null pointer dereference. Also, ensure that the destination buffer is properly null-terminated after the copy to avoid unterminated strings.\n\n```cpp\nif (name != nullptr && socket != nullptr) {\n    const char* src = socket->get_socket_id().c_str();\n    if (src != nullptr) {\n        strncpy(name, src, len);\n        if (len > 0) {\n            name[len - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n\n___\n"
              },
